From 7eceeaf144f3ae5496b8462bfbe39bacf1c946e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Garcia <44309076+ElGuslml@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:37:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] gpu: add an optional draw observer to the command
 processor

Tools that rebuild the guest's GPU state from somewhere else need to
compare their result with what the command processor actually executes.
XenosNative (a renderer that hooks the game's XDK Direct3D library) does
this in its bring-up phase: at every D3D draw it rebuilds the GPU state
from the D3D device structure, and checks it against the register file
the command processor has when it reaches that draw's packet.

IGraphicsSystem::SetDrawObserver(observer, user) registers a plain
callback that the command processor calls on the GPU thread for every
draw packet it executes (DRAW_INDX and DRAW_INDX_2, after predication).
It receives a GpuDrawInfo: the physical address of the packet header
(which matches the draw with the CPU call that wrote it), the opcode,
the register file, the bin mask and select of predicated tiling, whether
the draw was issued, and the bound shaders' ucode hashes, constant usage
maps and memexport use. The structure is plain data so that it crosses
the GPU plugin boundary; kGpuPluginAbiVersion is bumped because the
interface gained a virtual function.

With no observer set the cost is one relaxed atomic load per type-3
packet. Off by default.

This patch is only for projects that use XenosNative; it is kept in
xenos_native/sdk_patches/ and applied after the shared series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
